   "project": "fieldnotes",
   "reply": "I added `star INDEX` and made `list` put a `*` before starred notes. `python tools/check.py` passes: both unit tests and the line-length rule.\n\n- **Starring:** `star INDEX` sets `\"starred\": true` on that note, using the same 0-based positions that `list` shows, and prints `starred: <text>`. A non-numeric or out-of-range index prints an error and exits with code 1. The logic is `store.star()` in `fieldnotes/store.py`.\n- **Listing:** `list` now prints `*2026-\u2026  text` for starred notes. Unstarred notes print as before.\n- **CLI cleanup:** I moved the usage string into one `USAGE` constant in `fieldnotes/cli.py` so it mentions `star`.\n- **Tests:** I added `test_star` in `tests/test_store.py`, covering starring a note and the out-of-range case.\n\n`tools/check.py` requires `NOTES_HOME` to be set, so I ran it with a temporary directory. I didn't run the `star` command from the command line, and the `list` output and the CLI error path have no tests of their own.",
